WEBVTT

1
00:01:24.935 --> 00:01:26.111
Ron is down.

2
00:01:26.996 --> 00:01:28.728
He needs a medical evac.

3
00:01:28.799 --> 00:01:30.322
Where is it? Is it there?

4
00:01:30.572 --> 00:01:32.653
- Oh, the drive is gone.
- Are you sure?

5
00:01:37.001 --> 00:01:38.514
It's gone.
Give me a minute.

6
00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:40.845
They must have it.
Get off to them.

7
00:01:45.143 --> 00:01:47.879
- I'm stabilizing Ronson.
- We don't have the time.

8
00:01:47.929 --> 00:01:51.087
- I have to stop the bleeding.
- Leave him!

9
00:02:26.713 --> 00:02:27.666
Have you got him?

10
00:02:28.305 --> 00:02:29.957
He is in the black Audi.

11
00:02:30.614 --> 00:02:32.930
- What about Ronson.
- He's been hit.

12
00:02:32.995 --> 00:02:34.701
I'm sending an emergency
evacuation squad.

13
00:02:34.933 --> 00:02:37.060
Well, that'll be too bloody late.

14
00:02:37.814 --> 00:02:39.131
Have they seen us?

15
00:02:39.861 --> 00:02:43.373
Medical Evac for Ronson,
five minutes way.

16
00:02:48.476 --> 00:02:50.921
It's allright?
You'll wait using it.

17
00:02:52.673 --> 00:02:56.390
I wasn't using that one either.

18
00:03:40.123 --> 00:03:41.605
Keep your head down!

19
00:04:16.333 --> 00:04:17.628
Just get clear!

20
00:04:19.516 --> 00:04:20.921
Tanner, which way?

21
00:04:20.971 --> 00:04:22.912
Keep going.
I can direct you from here.

22
00:04:22.969 --> 00:04:24.231
We both know
what's at stake here.

23
00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:26.407
We can not afford
to lose that list.

24
00:04:26.497 --> 00:04:27.775
Yes, ma'am.

25
00:04:57.035 --> 00:04:58.283
Where are they now?

26
00:04:58.434 --> 00:05:01.240
They're on the top roof
of the grand bazaar.

27
00:05:52.883 --> 00:05:55.675
Take the left, there's a bridge.
You can cut him off.

28
00:06:47.493 --> 00:06:49.723
- What happened?
- They're on the train, ma' am.

29
00:06:49.773 --> 00:06:50.687
What do you mean
on the train?

30
00:06:50.712 --> 00:06:52.249
I mean they're on the top
of the train.

31
00:06:52.299 --> 00:06:54.455
Well, get off to them,
for God's sake.

32
00:07:24.378 --> 00:07:25.370
He's going out of range.

33
00:07:25.414 --> 00:07:26.944
We've lost tracking.
We are blind here.

34
00:07:27.082 --> 00:07:28.711
- What's going on?
- I'm still with them.

35
00:07:28.835 --> 00:07:31.263
There is CCTV satellite,
end of it.

36
00:08:21.389 --> 00:08:22.358
What was that?

37
00:08:22.988 --> 00:08:26.108
VW Beetles, I think.

38
00:08:52.223 --> 00:08:54.172
He's uncapping the cars.

39
00:09:31.849 --> 00:09:35.489
- 007, are you alright?
- Just changing carriages.

40
00:09:37.195 --> 00:09:38.494
What's going on?
Report!

41
00:09:38.612 --> 00:09:40.475
It's rather hard
to explain, ma'am.

42
00:09:40.701 --> 00:09:43.037
007 is saying proceed.

43
00:10:47.309 --> 00:10:50.932
This side here isn't much more road.
I do not think I can go any further.

44
00:11:25.763 --> 00:11:27.711
I may have a shot.

45
00:11:34.643 --> 00:11:35.536
It's not clean.

46
00:11:36.082 --> 00:11:38.231
Repeat.
I did not have a clean shot.

47
00:11:44.952 --> 00:11:47.109
There's a tunnel ahead.
I'm gonna lose them.

48
00:11:47.305 --> 00:11:50.490
- Can you get into a better position?
- Negative. There's no time.

49
00:11:52.572 --> 00:11:53.550
Take the shot.

50
00:11:55.689 --> 00:11:57.193
I said, "Take the shot!"

51
00:11:58.439 --> 00:12:00.519
Well, I can't.
I may get Bond.

52
00:12:00.569 --> 00:12:02.262
Take the bloody shot.

53
00:12:24.202 --> 00:12:25.358
Agent down.

54
00:16:33.575 --> 00:16:38.575
Sync and corrections by pinex
www.subscene.com

55
00:17:45.031 --> 00:17:47.285
It's like going
into the headmaster study.

56
00:17:47.335 --> 00:17:49.540
It's new chairman's
just a standard procedure.

57
00:17:49.882 --> 00:17:52.243
Bloody waste of my time,
that's what I'd call it.

58
00:17:52.334 --> 00:17:54.174
I'm sorry to have
to deal with such...

59
00:17:54.193 --> 00:17:56.051
a delicate subject
at our first encounter...

60
00:17:59.083 --> 00:18:00.225
But...

61
00:18:00.984 --> 00:18:03.315
I have to be frank with you.

62
00:18:03.365 --> 00:18:05.647
And it would be a good idea.

63
00:18:08.185 --> 00:18:09.648
The Prime Minister
is concerned.

64
00:18:10.738 --> 00:18:13.657
You can tell him my operatives
are pursuing every avenue.

65
00:18:13.868 --> 00:18:15.501
Have you considered
pulling up the agents?

66
00:18:15.707 --> 00:18:16.987
I've considered every option.

67
00:18:17.292 --> 00:18:19.259
Forgive me,
but that sounds like an evasion.

68
00:18:19.765 --> 00:18:21.618
Forgive me,
but why am I here?

69
00:18:23.015 --> 00:18:25.590
Three months ago
you lost the computer drive

70
00:18:25.615 --> 00:18:28.526
containing the identity
of almost every NATO agent

71
00:18:28.576 --> 00:18:31.924
embedded in terrorist organizations
across the globe.

72
00:18:32.758 --> 00:18:34.652
A list which,
in the eyes of our allies,

73
00:18:34.677 --> 00:18:35.922
never existed.

74
00:18:35.972 --> 00:18:39.522
So, if you'll forgive me,
I think you know why you're here.

75
00:18:39.572 --> 00:18:41.347
How you should call it,
a civilian oversight?

76
00:18:41.935 --> 00:18:43.483
No, what we call this is...

77
00:18:43.541 --> 00:18:45.657
a retirement planning.

78
00:18:46.879 --> 00:18:49.000
Your country has only
the highest respect for you

79
00:18:49.050 --> 00:18:51.021
and your many years
of service.

80
00:18:51.143 --> 00:18:52.686
When your current posting
is completed,

81
00:18:52.813 --> 00:18:55.070
you'll be awarded to JCMG

82
00:18:55.158 --> 00:18:56.796
with full honors.

83
00:18:57.588 --> 00:18:59.477
Congratulations.

84
00:19:00.347 --> 00:19:01.489
You are firing me?

85
00:19:01.514 --> 00:19:03.634
No, ma'am, I'm here to oversee
the transition period...

86
00:19:03.709 --> 00:19:06.877
leading to your voluntary retirement
in two months' time.

87
00:19:07.102 --> 00:19:09.413
Your successor has yet to be appointed,
so we'll be asking you...

88
00:19:09.587 --> 00:19:11.280
I'm not an idiot, Mallory.

89
00:19:12.200 --> 00:19:13.831
I know I can't do this job
forever.

90
00:19:14.525 --> 00:19:16.336
But I'll be damned if I'm going
to leave the department

91
00:19:16.365 --> 00:19:18.509
in worst shape than I found it.

92
00:19:18.884 --> 00:19:21.415
M... you've had a great run.

93
00:19:22.044 --> 00:19:24.834
- You should leave with dignity.
- Go to hell with dignity.

94
00:19:25.451 --> 00:19:28.670
I'll leave when the job's done.

95
00:19:45.731 --> 00:19:46.732
Yes?

96
00:19:48.980 --> 00:19:50.043
Now?

97
00:19:51.533 --> 00:19:53.015
Main alert from Q Robson,

98
00:19:53.170 --> 00:19:55.703
trying to decrypt
the stolen hard drive.

99
00:19:55.974 --> 00:19:58.417
We are tracing
the encryption signal.

100
00:19:58.467 --> 00:20:00.031
Localizing now.

101
00:20:02.422 --> 00:20:05.676
It's sent here in the UK.

102
00:20:06.146 --> 00:20:07.567
London.

103
00:20:08.030 --> 00:20:10.399
Get to inspect the basis
as soon as possible.

104
00:20:17.241 --> 00:20:19.409
- It's coming from MI6.
- What?

105
00:20:19.641 --> 00:20:22.448
The data back,
it is linking to our network.

106
00:20:22.483 --> 00:20:24.968
Corrupted.
This is behind our firewall.

107
00:20:25.104 --> 00:20:27.766
- We should shut down.
- No, track it.

108
00:20:27.791 --> 00:20:29.473
We have to know
where it's coming from.

109
00:20:30.203 --> 00:20:32.005
Strip the head
and try the source.

110
00:20:32.055 --> 00:20:33.898
How the hell
it entered in our system?

111
00:20:34.053 --> 00:20:36.110
Get in trace right now.

112
00:20:43.245 --> 00:20:46.687
- It is your computer, ma'am.
- Shut it down.

113
00:20:52.890 --> 00:20:54.211
What is this?

114
00:21:15.845 --> 00:21:17.257
For God's sake!

115
00:21:19.072 --> 00:21:20.194
Just get out of the way.

116
00:21:21.477 --> 00:21:22.967
- Don't you recognize the car?
- Madam...

117
00:24:48.377 --> 00:24:50.648
I'm gonna find
who ever did this.

118
00:25:39.844 --> 00:25:41.449
Where the hell
have you been?

119
00:25:42.482 --> 00:25:45.255
Enjoying death.

120
00:25:45.531 --> 00:25:48.785
007, reporting for duty.

121
00:25:55.704 --> 00:25:57.416
Why didn't you call?

122
00:25:57.992 --> 00:25:59.126
Didn't you get the postcard?

123
00:26:00.235 --> 00:26:01.191
You should try it sometimes.

124
00:26:01.411 --> 00:26:04.128
Get away from it all,
it really lends perspective.

125
00:26:04.385 --> 00:26:06.855
Run out of drink.
Were you awarded, eh?

126
00:26:06.905 --> 00:26:07.948
What it was you said?

127
00:26:08.439 --> 00:26:10.516
Take the bloody shot.

128
00:26:10.566 --> 00:26:12.528
I made a judgement call.

129
00:26:12.578 --> 00:26:15.004
You should have trusted me
to finish the job.

130
00:26:15.054 --> 00:26:16.481
It was the possibility
of losing you...

131
00:26:16.571 --> 00:26:19.520
or the certainty of losing
all those other agents.

132
00:26:19.670 --> 00:26:22.452
I made the only decision I could
and you know it.

133
00:26:23.583 --> 00:26:24.859
I think you've lost your nerve.

134
00:26:25.051 --> 00:26:27.271
What do you expect,
a bloody apology?

135
00:26:27.866 --> 00:26:30.816
You know the rules of the game.
You've been playing it long enough.

136
00:26:31.310 --> 00:26:34.366
- We both have.
- Maybe too long.

137
00:26:35.077 --> 00:26:38.662
Speak for yourself.

138
00:26:39.195 --> 00:26:40.974
Ronson didn't make it, did he?

139
00:26:42.303 --> 00:26:43.277
No.

140
00:26:46.769 --> 00:26:47.749
So, this is it.

141
00:26:48.636 --> 00:26:50.001
We are both played out.

142
00:26:51.380 --> 00:26:53.895
Well, if you believed that,
why did you come back?

143
00:26:54.150 --> 00:26:55.429
Good question.

144
00:26:57.188 --> 00:26:58.701
Because we are
under attack...

145
00:27:00.913 --> 00:27:03.799
and you know
we need you.

146
00:27:07.236 --> 00:27:08.527
Well, I'm here.

147
00:27:10.290 --> 00:27:11.369
You'll have to be debriefed...

148
00:27:11.462 --> 00:27:13.310
and declared fit
for active service.

149
00:27:14.625 --> 00:27:17.401
You're gonna return to duty
when you've passed the tests.

150
00:27:17.451 --> 00:27:18.643
So take them seriously.

151
00:27:19.747 --> 00:27:21.717
The shower
might be an order.

152
00:27:22.616 --> 00:27:24.747
I'm going home
and change.

153
00:27:24.797 --> 00:27:26.184
Oh, we sold your flat.

154
00:27:27.016 --> 00:27:28.622
Put your things
into storage.

155
00:27:29.496 --> 00:27:30.637
Standard procedure...

156
00:27:30.800 --> 00:27:34.207
on the death of an unmarried
employee with no next of kin.

157
00:27:34.960 --> 00:27:36.740
You should have called.

158
00:27:36.790 --> 00:27:38.360
I'll find a hotel.

159
00:27:38.876 --> 00:27:40.997
Well, you're bloody
will not sleep in here.

160
00:28:09.450 --> 00:28:11.827
They attacked into the
environmental control system

161
00:28:11.843 --> 00:28:15.095
locked out the safety protocols
and have turned on the gas.

162
00:28:15.145 --> 00:28:16.930
Well, that should
have been impossible.

163
00:28:17.177 --> 00:28:19.528
I was told that they have hacked
into our files.

164
00:28:19.779 --> 00:28:20.911
They knew her appointments.

165
00:28:21.058 --> 00:28:23.165
They knew she would be
out of the building.

166
00:28:23.215 --> 00:28:24.530
They weren't targeting her.

167
00:28:25.550 --> 00:28:27.544
They wanted us to see it.

168
00:28:28.786 --> 00:28:32.076
- Where are we, lieutenent?
- New digs.

169
00:28:39.418 --> 00:28:42.558
The old building was declared
strategically vulnerable.

170
00:28:42.923 --> 00:28:44.830
That's putting it marvelly.

171
00:28:44.855 --> 00:28:48.186
Their aim is to breach the most secured
computer system in Britain.

172
00:28:48.211 --> 00:28:50.568
So we are at war
with them now.

173
00:28:51.156 --> 00:28:53.421
This is part of Churchill's bunker.

174
00:28:53.471 --> 00:28:56.368
Some of these tunnels
are dating back to the 18th century.

175
00:28:56.386 --> 00:28:58.729
Quite fascinating,
if it wasn't for the rats.

176
00:28:58.951 --> 00:29:01.576
- When do I see M?
- Tomorrow, you'll see M...

177
00:29:02.313 --> 00:29:04.544
and Mallory too
if you're lucky.

178
00:29:04.594 --> 00:29:05.233
Who is Mallory?

179
00:29:05.412 --> 00:29:07.466
The new chairman of the
Intelligence and Security Committee.

180
00:29:07.813 --> 00:29:10.754
A charming man, I think.
You and him will really gonna hit it off.

181
00:29:13.161 --> 00:29:14.886
Welcome to the new MI6.

182
00:29:31.608 --> 00:29:33.851
We've have attempted to trace
the computer message, but...

183
00:29:34.379 --> 00:29:37.152
it was sent by an asymmetrical
security algorithm...

184
00:29:37.661 --> 00:29:39.036
with the chance to signal
all over the globe

185
00:29:39.088 --> 00:29:41.279
through thousands
of different servers.

186
00:29:41.346 --> 00:29:42.750
And now that they've accessed
M's code,

187
00:29:42.800 --> 00:29:45.555
it's only a matter of time before
they are able to decrypt the list.

188
00:29:45.635 --> 00:29:49.019
Q branch has been analyzing pictures.,
But so far, nothing.

189
00:29:49.155 --> 00:29:51.372
General feeling it's probably
something from her past

190
00:29:51.664 --> 00:29:53.873
Perhaps when she was
running things in Hong Kong.

191
00:29:54.374 --> 00:29:57.606
- It is no idea what it all means?
- And you believe that?

192
00:29:57.641 --> 00:30:00.684
The truth is we don't have
a clue of what's on the list...

193
00:30:00.709 --> 00:30:03.864
or what they are trying
to do with it.

194
00:30:09.637 --> 00:30:11.613
We can always do this later.

195
00:30:11.926 --> 00:30:15.314
You know what?
Let's.

196
00:31:21.738 --> 00:31:24.423
I'd like to start with some
simple words' sensations.

197
00:31:24.473 --> 00:31:27.107
Just tell me the first word
that punch into your head.

198
00:31:27.560 --> 00:31:29.567
For example I might day,
and you might say...

199
00:31:29.617 --> 00:31:31.593
Wasted.

200
00:31:35.456 --> 00:31:36.985
All right.

201
00:31:41.550 --> 00:31:42.331
Gun.

202
00:31:43.429 --> 00:31:44.062
Shot.

203
00:31:44.112 --> 00:31:46.150
- Agent.
- Provocative.

204
00:31:46.860 --> 00:31:48.596
- Woman.
- Provocatrix.

205
00:31:49.223 --> 00:31:51.725
- Heart.
- Target.

206
00:31:52.311 --> 00:31:54.616
- Bird.
- Sky.

207
00:31:54.666 --> 00:31:56.922
- M.
- Bitch.

208
00:31:59.907 --> 00:32:01.962
- Sunlight.
- Swim.

209
00:32:02.072 --> 00:32:03.699
- Moonlight.
- Dance.

210
00:32:04.021 --> 00:32:06.688
- Murder.
- Employment.

211
00:32:07.011 --> 00:32:08.662
- Country.
- England.

212
00:32:08.966 --> 00:32:10.680
Skyfall.

213
00:32:15.897 --> 00:32:17.404
Skyfall.

214
00:32:20.730 --> 00:32:22.977
Done.

215
00:32:28.180 --> 00:32:30.124
This is going well.

216
00:33:17.915 --> 00:33:19.228
Get these analyzed.

217
00:33:20.512 --> 00:33:22.366
When arrives, on me.

218
00:33:50.497 --> 00:33:51.533
She's ready for you.

219
00:33:52.546 --> 00:33:54.017
I'm sorry.
Have we met before?

220
00:33:55.499 --> 00:33:57.318
I am the one
who sould say "sorry".

221
00:33:59.998 --> 00:34:01.346
It was only four ribs.

222
00:34:02.062 --> 00:34:03.938
There's nonetheless
vital organs.

223
00:34:05.932 --> 00:34:07.952
Nothing major.

224
00:34:12.893 --> 00:34:14.544
No enough excitment
in Istambul?

225
00:34:14.720 --> 00:34:16.042
I've been reassigned.

226
00:34:16.108 --> 00:34:18.407
Temporary suspension
from field work.

227
00:34:18.559 --> 00:34:21.742
- Really?
- Something to do with killing 007.

228
00:34:21.959 --> 00:34:25.574
- Well, you gave it your best shot.
- It was hardly my best shot.

229
00:34:26.226 --> 00:34:27.946
I'm sure
I can survive your best.

230
00:34:28.381 --> 00:34:30.134
Time you'll get the chance.

231
00:34:30.159 --> 00:34:31.487
Would you do me a favor,
will you?

232
00:34:31.523 --> 00:34:33.619
If they'll do let you back
out there...

233
00:34:34.838 --> 00:34:36.740
Warn me first.

234
00:34:36.954 --> 00:34:39.543
I'm assisting Gareth Mallory
in the transition...

235
00:34:39.593 --> 00:34:41.795
and then I'll be back
in the field.

236
00:34:42.001 --> 00:34:44.538
- That's what you want?
- Yes, of course.

237
00:34:45.092 --> 00:34:47.814
- This is not for everyone.
- Ah, 007...

238
00:34:48.545 --> 00:34:49.986
It's this way.

239
00:34:50.011 --> 00:34:51.570
In your defense...

240
00:34:51.927 --> 00:34:54.615
a moving target
is much harder to hit.

241
00:34:55.799 --> 00:34:59.011
Then you better
keep moving.

242
00:35:09.068 --> 00:35:12.857
The whole office goes off in smoke
and that bloody thing survives.

243
00:35:12.885 --> 00:35:17.274
Your interior decorating tips
have always been appreciated, 007.

244
00:35:17.786 --> 00:35:19.889
007, Gareth Mallory.

245
00:35:19.939 --> 00:35:23.340
I hope I haven't miss anything
that P.M. does prattle in line of a crisis.

246
00:35:23.365 --> 00:35:26.046
- Bond.
- Mallory.

247
00:35:30.892 --> 00:35:33.040
I have just been reviewing
Bond's tests.

248
00:35:33.687 --> 00:35:36.882
Seems you passed.
Mind the scheme of your tiff?

249
00:35:37.374 --> 00:35:38.934
You're back
on active service.

250
00:35:40.247 --> 00:35:42.799
- Congratulations.
- Thank you.

251
00:35:44.813 --> 00:35:47.031
- I'll be outside.
- I may have one question.

252
00:35:48.462 --> 00:35:51.037
Why not stay dead?

253
00:35:51.788 --> 00:35:53.508
You have
the perfect way out.

254
00:35:53.558 --> 00:35:55.229
Go and live quietly
somewhere.

255
00:35:55.672 --> 00:35:59.155
Not many field agents
get to live this cleanly.

256
00:35:59.205 --> 00:36:01.110
Do you get out
in the field much?

257
00:36:02.011 --> 00:36:04.724
You don't need to be an operative
to see the obvious.

258
00:36:06.050 --> 00:36:07.824
It's a young men's game.

259
00:36:09.216 --> 00:36:10.378
Look, you've been
seriously injured.

260
00:36:10.429 --> 00:36:12.930
There's no shame in saying
you have lost a step.

261
00:36:13.243 --> 00:36:16.166
The only shame, it would be
not admitting until it's too late.

262
00:36:17.201 --> 00:36:20.794
I'm in, or fire me.
Entirely up to you.

263
00:36:21.032 --> 00:36:22.964
If he says he is ready,
he is ready.

264
00:36:24.202 --> 00:36:26.293
Perhaps
you can't see at all.

265
00:36:26.343 --> 00:36:27.122
Maybe you will.

266
00:36:27.172 --> 00:36:28.816
What exactly
are you implying?

267
00:36:29.275 --> 00:36:31.193
You are sentimental
about him.

268
00:36:32.484 --> 00:36:33.887
As long as I am the head
of this department,

269
00:36:34.311 --> 00:36:36.536
I'll choose my own
operatives.

270
00:36:38.285 --> 00:36:39.778
Fair enough.

271
00:36:44.210 --> 00:36:45.592
Good luck, 007.

272
00:36:47.001 --> 00:36:49.125
Don't cock it out.

273
00:36:54.816 --> 00:36:57.751
We've analyzed
these shrapnel fragments.

274
00:36:58.767 --> 00:37:01.611
You're lucky it wasn't a direct hit.
It would have cutted you in half.

275
00:37:01.939 --> 00:37:04.962
It's a depleted uranium shell.
A military grade.

276
00:37:05.940 --> 00:37:07.981
Hard to get,
extremely expensive

277
00:37:08.279 --> 00:37:11.750
and only used by select few.

278
00:37:11.800 --> 00:37:13.192
You recognize anyone?

279
00:37:14.904 --> 00:37:16.226
Him.

280
00:37:17.180 --> 00:37:19.324
Okay, the name is Patrice.

281
00:37:19.650 --> 00:37:20.347
He's a ghost.

282
00:37:20.397 --> 00:37:22.225
An unknown resident
without country of origin.

283
00:37:22.259 --> 00:37:23.818
How do we find him?

284
00:37:23.868 --> 00:37:27.154
Well, luckily I used to have one
or two friends left in the CIA.

285
00:37:27.469 --> 00:37:30.060
They're after him for the Yemeni
ambassador's murder.

286
00:37:30.110 --> 00:37:31.343
And they're getting close.

287
00:37:31.393 --> 00:37:35.425
Intel is he's gonna be in Shanghai
in two days time. Probably a new job.

288
00:37:35.705 --> 00:37:38.005
You have to go there
and wait further instructions.

289
00:37:38.056 --> 00:37:40.030
If he turns up, it's yours.

290
00:37:40.080 --> 00:37:43.345
Find out who he worked for
and who has the list.

291
00:37:43.829 --> 00:37:47.134
- Then, terminate him for Ronson.
- With pleasure.

292
00:37:48.155 --> 00:37:51.367
Is there anything else
you want to tell me?

293
00:37:52.160 --> 00:37:53.788
No.

294
00:37:53.838 --> 00:37:56.703
Report to the new quarter master
for a few documentation.

295
00:37:57.043 --> 00:38:00.606
He hasn't set up sharp yet, but
Tanner will put you two together.

296
00:38:00.656 --> 00:38:01.782
Good luck.

297
00:38:02.145 --> 00:38:03.552
Thank you.

298
00:38:07.230 --> 00:38:08.571
007...

299
00:38:10.604 --> 00:38:12.197
You are ready for this?

300
00:38:13.465 --> 00:38:14.797
Yes, ma'am.

301
00:38:18.572 --> 00:38:19.967
I didn't know
Bond passed the tests.

302
00:38:21.081 --> 00:38:22.750
He didn't.

303
00:38:52.174 --> 00:38:54.297
Always makes me feel
a little melancholy.

304
00:38:54.880 --> 00:38:58.964
A grand whole warship being
ignominiously hold the way to scrap.

305
00:39:01.750 --> 00:39:04.420
Inevitabilty of time,
don't you think?

306
00:39:06.813 --> 00:39:08.127
What do you see?

307
00:39:09.910 --> 00:39:11.784
A bloody big ship.

308
00:39:12.978 --> 00:39:14.156
Excuse me.

309
00:39:14.616 --> 00:39:15.784
007...

310
00:39:17.157 --> 00:39:18.695
I'm your new
Quarter master.

311
00:39:20.656 --> 00:39:22.480
You must be joking.

312
00:39:23.205 --> 00:39:24.952
Why, because I'm not wearing
a lab coat?

313
00:39:25.167 --> 00:39:27.428
Because you still have spots.

314
00:39:28.268 --> 00:39:29.971
My complexion
is hardly relevant.

315
00:39:29.986 --> 00:39:31.459
And your confidence is.

316
00:39:33.017 --> 00:39:34.770
Age is no guarantee
of efficiency.

317
00:39:34.896 --> 00:39:37.285
And youth is no guarantee
of innovation.

318
00:39:38.210 --> 00:39:40.345
Oh, how's it I can do more damage
on my laptop

319
00:39:40.370 --> 00:39:43.247
sitting in my pyjamas before
my first cup of Old Grey

320
00:39:43.272 --> 00:39:45.268
than you could do
in a year in the field.

321
00:39:45.293 --> 00:39:46.951
So why do you need me?

322
00:39:48.273 --> 00:39:50.538
Every now and then
a trigger has to be pulled.

323
00:39:51.370 --> 00:39:53.159
Or not pulled.

324
00:39:53.664 --> 00:39:56.786
It is hard to know which
in your pyjamas.

325
00:40:00.158 --> 00:40:05.415
- Q...
- 007.

326
00:40:08.048 --> 00:40:09.920
Ticket to Shanghai.

327
00:40:09.970 --> 00:40:12.173
- Documentation and passport.
- Thank you.

328
00:40:12.208 --> 00:40:15.427
And this.

329
00:40:17.699 --> 00:40:20.455
Walter PPK, it's 9mm short.

330
00:40:21.185 --> 00:40:23.334
There's a microdermal sensor
in the grip...

331
00:40:24.220 --> 00:40:27.203
encoded to your palm print,
so only you can fire it.

332
00:40:27.984 --> 00:40:31.548
That's a random killing machine
more than a personal statement.

333
00:40:32.199 --> 00:40:33.559
And this?

334
00:40:34.957 --> 00:40:37.415
Standard as your
radio transmitter.

335
00:40:37.822 --> 00:40:40.788
Activated and broadcast
your own location.

336
00:40:41.513 --> 00:40:42.758
Distress it.

337
00:40:44.351 --> 00:40:47.428
And that's it.

338
00:40:48.224 --> 00:40:51.567
A gun, and a radio.

339
00:40:53.878 --> 00:40:55.603
Not exactly Christmas, isn't it?

340
00:40:56.715 --> 00:40:59.213
Were you expecting
an exploding pen?

341
00:41:00.861 --> 00:41:03.022
We don't really go in
for that anymore.

342
00:41:10.901 --> 00:41:12.531
Good luck out there
on the field.

343
00:41:13.050 --> 00:41:15.928
And please return
the equipment in one piece.

344
00:41:21.316 --> 00:41:23.030
Brave new world.

345
00:49:42.963 --> 00:49:44.576
Who got the list.

346
00:49:49.171 --> 00:49:51.585
Tell me, who you working for.

347
00:51:20.850 --> 00:51:23.432
Tanner, he has posted
the first five names.

348
00:51:24.293 --> 00:51:25.180
Their cover is blown.

349
00:51:25.595 --> 00:51:27.884
They're in danger.
Get them out now.

350
00:52:07.184 --> 00:52:08.438
Room service.

351
00:52:17.544 --> 00:52:18.942
I didn't order anything.

352
00:52:19.464 --> 00:52:20.600
Not even you.

353
00:52:20.843 --> 00:52:22.472
I have got some
new information.

354
00:52:23.554 --> 00:52:26.723
Are not you a little too qualified
to be delivering messages?

355
00:52:27.703 --> 00:52:29.839
It's all part
of the learning curve.

356
00:52:30.242 --> 00:52:32.217
And Q is afraid of flying.

357
00:52:34.745 --> 00:52:38.624
So, whoever stole the list
has already decrypted it.

358
00:52:39.255 --> 00:52:41.746
They posted the first five names
on the web.

359
00:52:41.796 --> 00:52:45.187
- It was only a matter of time.
- That should be the start.

360
00:52:45.237 --> 00:52:48.579
They're posting five more
next week and the week after.

361
00:52:49.486 --> 00:52:51.658
It's some kind of
sadistic game.

362
00:52:56.449 --> 00:52:58.071
Cut through razor.

363
00:52:59.709 --> 00:53:01.504
How very traditional.

364
00:53:02.801 --> 00:53:05.873
Well, I'm going to do some things
the old-fashion way.

365
00:53:08.188 --> 00:53:10.808
Sometimes the old ways
are the best.

366
00:53:21.400 --> 00:53:23.771
Are you putting your life
in my hands again?

367
00:53:26.468 --> 00:53:31.089
Tans, already briefed me
on the list...

368
00:53:32.544 --> 00:53:36.627
raising the tantalizing question
of what you are really doing here.

369
00:53:37.919 --> 00:53:40.850
The official directive
was to help...

370
00:53:42.227 --> 00:53:45.639
in anyway I can.

371
00:53:45.801 --> 00:53:48.549
Like spying for Mallory.

372
00:53:50.260 --> 00:53:52.498
You know, Mallory
is not as bad as you think.

373
00:53:54.073 --> 00:53:56.218
He is a bureaucrat.

374
00:53:56.776 --> 00:53:58.657
You should do
your homework.

375
00:53:59.598 --> 00:54:01.520
Gareth Mallory
was Lieutenant Colonel...

376
00:54:01.570 --> 00:54:04.772
Lieutenant Colonel in Northern
Ireland Herford regiment.

377
00:54:04.822 --> 00:54:07.457
He spent three months
at the hands of the IRA.

378
00:54:09.012 --> 00:54:11.487
So there's more to him
that meets the eye.

379
00:54:14.638 --> 00:54:16.124
We'll see.

380
00:54:17.832 --> 00:54:19.343
Keep still.

381
00:54:21.574 --> 00:54:24.174
This is the tricky part.

382
00:54:35.669 --> 00:54:37.624
That's better.

383
00:54:38.479 --> 00:54:41.375
- You know the part now.
- Mmh, mmh.

384
00:54:43.409 --> 00:54:45.052
And what part is that?

385
00:54:47.227 --> 00:54:48.590
Old dog...

386
00:54:49.621 --> 00:54:51.910
new tricks.

387
00:56:03.526 --> 00:56:04.764
Good evening.

388
00:56:05.268 --> 00:56:06.490
Good evening.

389
00:56:06.540 --> 00:56:08.602
Don't you touch your ear.

390
00:56:09.689 --> 00:56:11.151
There are three exits.

391
00:56:12.456 --> 00:56:14.475
And lots of blind spots.

392
00:56:15.027 --> 00:56:16.949
I've got them covered.

393
00:56:22.819 --> 00:56:24.251
You look beautiful
in that dress.

394
00:56:25.222 --> 00:56:26.454
You could scrub out
about yourself.

395
00:56:26.570 --> 00:56:29.682
It's amazing what one could do
with an extra pair of hands.

396
00:56:30.000 --> 00:56:31.592
You're telling mean.

397
00:56:33.360 --> 00:56:34.422
You gamble?

398
00:56:34.944 --> 00:56:37.417
Don't like you a little flatten
now and then?

399
00:56:39.403 --> 00:56:41.808
He doesn't like
to take chances.

400
00:56:47.250 --> 00:56:49.212
Good evening, sir.
How may I help you?

401
00:56:49.362 --> 00:56:51.131
I'd like to cash thes in,
please.

402
00:56:58.061 --> 00:56:59.430
One moment, sir.

403
00:57:31.931 --> 00:57:34.080
Good fortune tonight, sir.

404
00:57:39.740 --> 00:57:41.377
Let's hope so.

405
00:57:50.221 --> 00:57:52.205
With compliments
of the house.

406
00:57:53.082 --> 00:57:54.669
Thank you.

407
00:58:14.527 --> 00:58:16.802
Now you can afford
to buy me a drink?

408
00:58:19.362 --> 00:58:21.886
Maybe I could give
a stretch or two.

409
00:58:23.233 --> 00:58:26.168
I guess I got good
4 million euros in here.

410
00:58:26.634 --> 00:58:27.803
Not bad.

411
00:58:27.928 --> 00:58:30.854
- I like this game.
- Why don't we play another?

412
00:58:31.995 --> 00:58:33.464
I don't gamble.

413
00:58:36.962 --> 00:58:38.630
I'm not very lucky.

414
00:58:39.067 --> 00:58:41.478
With lucky old friend
in Shanghai.

415
00:58:45.227 --> 00:58:48.351
I've been waiting to see
who'll redeem the chip.

416
00:58:48.875 --> 00:58:52.575
You made such a gold entrance
into our little drama.

417
00:58:52.719 --> 00:58:54.878
Do I have
a complicated plot?

418
00:58:56.011 --> 00:58:58.248
Who doesnt't appreciate
the occasion of twists?

419
00:58:58.716 --> 00:59:03.157
- Mr...
- Bond. James Bond.

420
00:59:03.667 --> 00:59:06.734
Severing,
so Mr. Bond...

421
00:59:06.784 --> 00:59:10.206
shall we discuss your next
performance with all that drink?

422
00:59:10.411 --> 00:59:11.975
Not bad.

423
00:59:14.766 --> 00:59:18.135
Are your friends
be joining us?

424
00:59:18.927 --> 00:59:22.140
I'm afraid... it's inevitable.

425
00:59:25.575 --> 00:59:27.816
- She's pretty.
- No, no.

426
00:59:27.874 --> 00:59:30.902
Do you like that ass,
don't you think?

427
00:59:30.952 --> 00:59:32.425
Well, I'll keep you posted.

428
00:59:44.065 --> 00:59:45.362
Perfect.

429
00:59:47.697 --> 00:59:50.388
Would you mind if I ask you
a business question?

430
00:59:51.974 --> 00:59:54.688
Depends on the question.

431
00:59:54.738 --> 00:59:57.404
It has to do with... death.

432
00:59:58.305 --> 01:00:00.516
A subject in which
you're well versed.

433
01:00:01.342 --> 01:00:03.349
How would you know that?

434
01:00:04.496 --> 01:00:07.404
Only a certain kind of woman
wears a backless dress

435
01:00:07.429 --> 01:00:10.436
with a Beretta .70
strapped to her thigh.

436
01:00:11.058 --> 01:00:13.703
One could never be
too careful when...

437
01:00:13.704 --> 01:00:16.706
a handsome man in tuxedos
carry Walters...

438
01:00:19.244 --> 01:00:22.176
I'm correct in assuming
you'll killed Patrice?

439
01:00:23.383 --> 01:00:24.565
Yes.

440
01:00:26.215 --> 01:00:28.064
Might I ask why?

441
01:00:29.387 --> 01:00:31.517
I want to meet
your employer.

442
01:00:43.623 --> 01:00:47.166
Be careful
what you wish for.

443
01:00:47.664 --> 01:00:49.095
You are scared.

444
01:00:50.212 --> 01:00:52.241
Thank you
for the drink...

445
01:00:53.909 --> 01:00:55.392
Mr. Bond.

446
01:01:03.325 --> 01:01:05.013
You put on a good show.

447
01:01:07.345 --> 01:01:08.793
But ever since
we sat down here

448
01:01:09.015 --> 01:01:11.790
you haven't stop looking
at your bodyguards.

449
01:01:13.268 --> 01:01:15.529
The three of them
have been excessive.

450
01:01:16.007 --> 01:01:17.720
They're controlling you.

451
01:01:18.214 --> 01:01:19.628
They're not protecting you.

452
01:01:21.817 --> 01:01:23.120
Tattoo on your wrist...

453
01:01:23.688 --> 01:01:25.125
is Macao's sex trade..

454
01:01:25.217 --> 01:01:28.286
You belonged to one of the houses
when were you, 12?

455
01:01:28.859 --> 01:01:30.452
13?

456
01:01:31.391 --> 01:01:33.405
I can see images
of a way out.

457
01:01:34.194 --> 01:01:36.797
I hope she told
you were in love.

458
01:01:38.166 --> 01:01:40.842
But that was a long time ago.

459
01:01:42.964 --> 01:01:45.011
You know nothing about it.

460
01:01:45.539 --> 01:01:49.005
Right, when a woman is afraid
and pretending not to be.

461
01:01:52.223 --> 01:01:54.200
How much do you know
about fear?

462
01:01:54.761 --> 01:01:57.019
All there is.

463
01:01:57.824 --> 01:01:59.624
Not like this.

464
01:02:00.392 --> 01:02:05.255
And... not like him.

465
01:02:05.305 --> 01:02:06.764
I can help you.

466
01:02:07.603 --> 01:02:10.371
- I don't think so.
- Let me try.

467
01:02:12.657 --> 01:02:13.982
How?

468
01:02:15.018 --> 01:02:16.668
Bring me to him.

469
01:02:19.344 --> 01:02:23.006
- Can you kill him?
- Yes.

470
01:02:23.313 --> 01:02:27.012
- Will you?
- Someone usually dies.

471
01:02:31.648 --> 01:02:35.022
Perhaps you can.

472
01:02:41.268 --> 01:02:43.281
When I leave,
they're going to kill you.

473
01:02:44.573 --> 01:02:47.274
If you survive,
I'm on the Kimera.

474
01:02:47.754 --> 01:02:48.941
North Harbour...

475
01:02:49.798 --> 01:02:51.463
Berth 7.

476
01:02:52.616 --> 01:02:56.007
We cast off in an hour.

477
01:03:00.324 --> 01:03:02.732
Very nice to have met you,
Mr. Bond.

478
01:03:04.384 --> 01:03:05.794
Good luck.

479
01:04:31.527 --> 01:04:33.263
Good luck with that.

480
01:04:57.512 --> 01:04:58.670
Thank you.

481
01:05:03.379 --> 01:05:05.573
Put it all on red.

482
01:05:07.698 --> 01:05:10.030
That's the circle of life.

483
01:05:33.957 --> 01:05:35.295
Yes?

484
01:05:38.906 --> 01:05:41.994
It's time to cast off.

485
01:05:42.594 --> 01:05:44.034
All right.

486
01:06:39.521 --> 01:06:42.041
I like you better
without putting you on red.

487
01:06:45.809 --> 01:06:49.861
I feel naked without it.

488
01:07:05.275 --> 01:07:05.965
Good evening.

489
01:07:06.089 --> 01:07:07.832
The controversy surrounding
the Ministry of Defence...

490
01:07:07.957 --> 01:07:09.415
has excalated today

491
01:07:09.661 --> 01:07:13.330
as images of the Hussein
assassination continue to circulate.

492
01:07:13.587 --> 01:07:17.100
We should warn you, some viewers
might find these images disturbing.

493
01:07:18.621 --> 01:07:22.061
Captain Hussein, an MI6 operative
embedded in the Middle East

494
01:07:22.269 --> 01:07:25.803
was one of the five agents exposed
in what is now been considered

495
01:07:26.079 --> 01:07:29.844
the greatest internal security breach
in modern British history.

496
01:07:30.115 --> 01:07:33.746
The Prime Minister continues
to express public support for MI6

497
01:07:34.158 --> 01:07:36.104
while the opposition has taken
the position...

498
01:07:36.154 --> 01:07:38.723
has taken the position where a bunch
of antiquate bloody idiots

499
01:07:38.875 --> 01:07:42.054
are fighting a war we don't understand
and can't possibly win.

500
01:07:42.512 --> 01:07:44.680
Look, three of my agents
are dead already.

501
01:07:44.840 --> 01:07:46.921
Don't you bring me
in politics now.

502
01:07:46.946 --> 01:07:48.196
The Prime Minister
has ordered an enquiry.

503
01:07:48.558 --> 01:07:49.768
You'll have to appear.

504
01:07:49.817 --> 01:07:53.326
Standing in the stocks of midday?
Who is antiquated now?

505
01:07:53.351 --> 01:07:55.528
For Christ sake, listen to yourself.
We are a democracy

506
01:07:55.529 --> 01:07:58.060
and are accountable to the people
we are trying to defend.

507
01:07:58.085 --> 01:07:59.506
We can't keep working
in the shadows.

508
01:07:59.557 --> 01:08:01.894
There are no more shadows.

509
01:08:01.919 --> 01:08:03.746
You don't get this, do you.

510
01:08:04.597 --> 01:08:07.501
Whoever is behind this,
whoever is doing it, he knows us.

511
01:08:08.194 --> 01:08:09.308
He is one of us.

512
01:08:09.559 --> 01:08:11.425
He comes from
the same place as Bond.

513
01:08:11.450 --> 01:08:14.007
The place you say
doesn't exist.

514
01:08:14.549 --> 01:08:16.309
The shadows.

515
01:08:53.480 --> 01:08:55.276
It's not too late.

516
01:09:41.747 --> 01:09:43.979
They abandoned it
almost in the night.

517
01:09:45.446 --> 01:09:48.837
He made them think there was
a leak at the chemical plant.

518
01:09:50.271 --> 01:09:54.212
It is amazing the panic you can
cause with a single computer.

519
01:09:54.680 --> 01:09:56.613
He wanted the island.

520
01:09:56.732 --> 01:09:58.639
So he took it.

521
01:09:59.692 --> 01:10:01.811
Does he always get
what he wants?

522
01:10:02.968 --> 01:10:04.853
More than you know.

523
01:10:08.563 --> 01:10:09.783
I'm sorry.

524
01:10:38.208 --> 01:10:41.138
Hello, James.
Welcome.

525
01:10:41.484 --> 01:10:42.989
You like the island?

526
01:10:46.563 --> 01:10:48.099
My grandmother
had an island.

527
01:10:48.701 --> 01:10:49.825
Nothing to boast off.

528
01:10:50.204 --> 01:10:51.907
You could walk along
within an hour.

529
01:10:52.146 --> 01:10:54.583
But still it was,
it was a paradise for us.

530
01:10:55.945 --> 01:10:58.154
One summer,
we went for a visit...

531
01:10:58.386 --> 01:11:02.001
and discovered the place
had been infested with rats.

532
01:11:02.732 --> 01:11:06.244
They'd come on a fishing boat
and gorged themselves on coconut.

533
01:11:07.334 --> 01:11:10.852
So, how do you get rid
of the rats on an island?

534
01:11:10.902 --> 01:11:12.122
My grandmother showed me.

535
01:11:13.279 --> 01:11:15.846
We buried an whole drum
and changed the lead.

536
01:11:16.146 --> 01:11:18.139
Then we wired the coconut
to the lead as bait...

537
01:11:18.354 --> 01:11:22.026
and the rats will come
for the coconut, and...

538
01:11:22.317 --> 01:11:23.804
They would fall
into the drum.

539
01:11:25.047 --> 01:11:29.144
And after a month
you've trapped all the rats.

540
01:11:29.389 --> 01:11:32.007
But what did you do then?

541
01:11:32.057 --> 01:11:34.060
Throw the drum
into the ocean?

542
01:11:34.769 --> 01:11:36.917
Burn it? No...

543
01:11:37.485 --> 01:11:39.178
You just leave it...

544
01:11:40.445 --> 01:11:42.761
and they begin
to get hungry.

545
01:11:43.627 --> 01:11:47.439
And one by one...

546
01:11:47.590 --> 01:11:49.505
they start
eating each other...

547
01:11:49.555 --> 01:11:53.299
until there are only two left,
the two survivors.

548
01:11:53.676 --> 01:11:55.889
And then what,
do you kill them? No.

549
01:11:56.555 --> 01:11:59.658
You take them
and release them into the trees.

550
01:12:00.050 --> 01:12:02.622
And now they don't eat
coconut anymore.

551
01:12:03.314 --> 01:12:05.720
Now they only eat rat.

552
01:12:06.947 --> 01:12:09.511
You have changed
their nature.

553
01:12:11.454 --> 01:12:12.864
The two survivors.

554
01:12:13.860 --> 01:12:16.104
This is what you made us.

555
01:12:18.137 --> 01:12:20.234
I made my own choices.

556
01:12:21.203 --> 01:12:22.826
You think you did.

557
01:12:23.894 --> 01:12:25.456
That's sheer genius.

558
01:12:27.463 --> 01:12:28.952
Station H.

559
01:12:29.865 --> 01:12:31.548
Am I right, Hong Kong?

560
01:12:32.742 --> 01:12:34.866
'86 to '97.

561
01:12:35.840 --> 01:12:37.802
Back then,
I was her favorite.

562
01:12:38.047 --> 01:12:39.729
And you're not nearly
the agent I was.

563
01:12:39.890 --> 01:12:41.450
I can tell you that.

564
01:12:43.220 --> 01:12:44.069
Just look at you.

565
01:12:44.070 --> 01:12:47.265
Barely held together
by your pills, and your drink.

566
01:12:47.266 --> 01:12:49.922
Don't forget my pathetic
love of country.

567
01:12:52.003 --> 01:12:54.931
You're still clinging to your faith
in that old woman

568
01:12:55.804 --> 01:12:58.312
- when all she does is lie to you.
- She never lied lied to me.

569
01:12:58.362 --> 01:13:00.233
- No?
- No.

570
01:13:00.406 --> 01:13:02.477
What do you score on your
maximum ship evaluation?

571
01:13:02.478 --> 01:13:04.233
70.

572
01:13:04.984 --> 01:13:06.530
40.

573
01:13:08.538 --> 01:13:10.808
Did she tell you the psychologyst
cleaned you for duty?

574
01:13:10.809 --> 01:13:12.079
- Yes.
- No.

575
01:13:12.710 --> 01:13:13.581
No.

576
01:13:22.191 --> 01:13:24.135
Medical evaluation; Fail.

577
01:13:24.216 --> 01:13:26.170
Physical evalution; Fail.

578
01:13:26.541 --> 01:13:32.241
Psychological evaluation, alcohol
and substance addiction indicated.

579
01:13:33.840 --> 01:13:35.577
Pathological rejection
of authority

580
01:13:35.628 --> 01:13:38.882
based on unresolved
childhood trauma.

581
01:13:44.673 --> 01:13:47.313
Subject is not approved
for field duty

582
01:13:47.363 --> 01:13:50.559
and immediate suspension
from service advised.

583
01:13:50.648 --> 01:13:52.664
What is this,
if not betrayal?

584
01:13:53.041 --> 01:13:55.570
She send you off to me,
knowing that you're not ready

585
01:13:55.582 --> 01:13:56.794
knowing you will likely die.

586
01:13:57.229 --> 01:13:59.683
Mommy was very bad.

587
01:14:23.488 --> 01:14:25.567
See what she's done to you?

588
01:14:26.643 --> 01:14:29.917
Well, she never tied me
to a chair.

589
01:14:29.968 --> 01:14:34.352
I loss.

590
01:14:35.109 --> 01:14:37.514
Are you sure
this is about her?

591
01:14:37.618 --> 01:14:39.256
It's about her...

592
01:14:39.823 --> 01:14:42.428
and you and me.

593
01:14:43.371 --> 01:14:45.679
You see,
we are last two rats.

594
01:14:46.442 --> 01:14:48.358
We can either
eat each other.

595
01:14:55.707 --> 01:14:57.256
Or eat everyone else.

596
01:14:59.846 --> 01:15:03.376
How you're trying to remember
your training now?

597
01:15:04.810 --> 01:15:07.476
What's the regulation
to cover this?

598
01:15:10.636 --> 01:15:13.033
Well, first time
for everything.

599
01:15:13.640 --> 01:15:14.635
Yes.

600
01:15:16.804 --> 01:15:19.728
What makes you think
this is my first time?

601
01:15:20.854 --> 01:15:24.726
Oh, Mr. Bond...

602
01:15:25.333 --> 01:15:29.133
All the physical stuff's so dull.
So dull.

603
01:15:32.128 --> 01:15:33.467
Changing spies.

604
01:15:34.037 --> 01:15:35.796
So old-fashioned.

605
01:15:38.906 --> 01:15:40.699
Your knees
must be killing you.

606
01:15:45.619 --> 01:15:46.797
England...

607
01:15:47.664 --> 01:15:50.117
the Empire, MI6.

608
01:15:50.529 --> 01:15:52.358
You're living
in the ruins as well.

609
01:15:52.789 --> 01:15:54.252
You just don't know it yet.

610
01:15:55.567 --> 01:15:58.084
At least here there are no
old ladies giving orders...

611
01:15:58.294 --> 01:16:01.073
and no little...

612
01:16:02.327 --> 01:16:05.120
gadgets from those fools
in Q print.

613
01:16:07.751 --> 01:16:08.939
If you'd want it,

614
01:16:09.536 --> 01:16:11.914
you could pick
your own secret missions...

615
01:16:11.964 --> 01:16:13.890
as I do.

616
01:16:14.942 --> 01:16:15.918
Name it.

617
01:16:17.242 --> 01:16:18.859
Name it.

618
01:16:21.111 --> 01:16:25.638
You destabilize a multinational
by manipulating stocks. Easy.

619
01:16:26.574 --> 01:16:30.191
Interrupt transmission
from a spy satellite over Kabul.

620
01:16:30.226 --> 01:16:31.792
Done.

621
01:16:31.842 --> 01:16:35.804
Rig an election in Uganda.
All to the highest bidder.

622
01:16:35.963 --> 01:16:37.920
Or a gas explosion in London.

623
01:16:39.351 --> 01:16:41.429
Guess the point, anglic.

624
01:16:41.479 --> 01:16:44.822
Well, everyone needs a hobby.

625
01:16:48.975 --> 01:16:51.840
So what's yours?

626
01:16:53.186 --> 01:16:56.851
Resurrection.

627
01:16:58.770 --> 01:17:00.681
Let me show you something.

628
01:17:13.241 --> 01:17:16.050
Tells a story, doesn't it?

629
01:17:19.181 --> 01:17:21.006
They left the island so quickly

630
01:17:21.350 --> 01:17:25.041
that couldn't decide what to take
what to leave, what was important.

631
01:17:25.808 --> 01:17:29.240
And this every day reminds me
to focus on the essentials.

632
01:17:29.574 --> 01:17:33.457
There is nothing...
nothing superflous in my life.

633
01:17:33.719 --> 01:17:37.099
When a thing is redundant,
it is... eliminated.

634
01:17:47.483 --> 01:17:49.106
Fifty years old McCullan.

635
01:17:50.189 --> 01:17:52.760
A particular favorite of yours,
I understand?

636
01:17:55.082 --> 01:17:57.749
So... what's the toast?

637
01:18:00.369 --> 01:18:02.697
To the women we love?

638
01:18:13.205 --> 01:18:14.139
Darling...

639
01:18:15.497 --> 01:18:18.439
Darling,
your love is out here.

640
01:18:23.725 --> 01:18:24.680
No, no, no, no...

641
01:18:25.746 --> 01:18:27.868
Stand up straight,
keep still...

642
01:18:30.016 --> 01:18:31.402
and whatever you do,
don't lose your head.

643
01:18:31.793 --> 01:18:34.642
Don't lose your head.

644
01:18:36.932 --> 01:18:38.533
Don't lose your head.

645
01:18:39.844 --> 01:18:42.827
Time to redeem
your maximum ship scores.

646
01:18:44.819 --> 01:18:45.762
Let's see.

647
01:18:46.671 --> 01:18:47.866
You can be the first...

648
01:18:48.844 --> 01:18:51.643
to knock the gloss
from her head.

649
01:18:57.333 --> 01:19:00.113
And just to be sporting,
I'll let you go first.

650
01:19:18.177 --> 01:19:19.914
Let's see
who it's up on top.

651
01:19:33.234 --> 01:19:34.901
Oh, can't believe it.

652
01:19:35.544 --> 01:19:37.241
Can't believe it.

653
01:19:37.600 --> 01:19:39.248
Did you really die that day?

654
01:19:39.945 --> 01:19:43.977
Is there any,
any of the old 007 left?

655
01:19:52.539 --> 01:19:54.003
My turn.

656
01:19:57.532 --> 01:20:00.177
I win.
What do you say to that?

657
01:20:03.759 --> 01:20:05.133
So waste of good scotch.

658
01:20:16.166 --> 01:20:17.569
What are you
going to do now?

659
01:20:17.755 --> 01:20:20.192
Take me back to her?
All on your own?

660
01:20:20.805 --> 01:20:22.704
Who says
I'm on my own?

661
01:20:41.583 --> 01:20:43.361
Latest thing
from Q branch.

662
01:20:44.656 --> 01:20:46.504
On the radio.

663
01:21:41.857 --> 01:21:43.979
You are smaller
than I remembered.

664
01:21:45.233 --> 01:21:47.444
Well, as I bet you remember
you were tall.

665
01:21:47.521 --> 01:21:51.036
Strange, for me it feels just...
like yesterday.

666
01:21:52.948 --> 01:21:55.788
- Are you surprised?
- Not particularly.

667
01:21:55.871 --> 01:21:58.131
But then you always were
a slippery one.

668
01:21:58.293 --> 01:22:00.736
Maybe that's why
you liked me so much.

669
01:22:00.786 --> 01:22:04.476
- You flatter yourself.
- No remorse.

670
01:22:06.302 --> 01:22:08.676
Just as I can imagine it.

671
01:22:09.261 --> 01:22:11.511
Regret is unprofessional.

672
01:22:17.744 --> 01:22:18.898
"Regret is unprofessional"...

673
01:22:19.186 --> 01:22:23.164
They kept for five months
in a room with no air.

674
01:22:23.214 --> 01:22:24.055
They tortured me.

675
01:22:24.822 --> 01:22:27.990
And I ain't protected your secrets.
I protected you.

676
01:22:28.973 --> 01:22:30.651
But they made me suffer...

677
01:22:30.886 --> 01:22:32.292
and suffer...

678
01:22:33.745 --> 01:22:35.356
and suffer.

679
01:22:36.503 --> 01:22:38.171
Until I realized...

680
01:22:39.917 --> 01:22:42.547
it was you...
who betrayed me.

681
01:22:43.631 --> 01:22:45.350
You betrayed me.

682
01:22:46.736 --> 01:22:49.659
So I had only one thing left.

683
01:22:51.539 --> 01:22:55.161
My cyanide capsule
in my back lift molar.

684
01:22:55.211 --> 01:22:58.212
You remember, right?

685
01:23:01.358 --> 01:23:03.114
So I broke the tooth...

686
01:23:04.481 --> 01:23:07.158
and bit into the capsule.

687
01:23:11.856 --> 01:23:14.018
Burned all my insights...

688
01:23:14.985 --> 01:23:16.511
but I didn't die.

689
01:23:20.006 --> 01:23:22.228
Life climed to me
like a disease.

690
01:23:27.224 --> 01:23:28.286
And then...

691
01:23:28.506 --> 01:23:29.934
I understood...

692
01:23:30.167 --> 01:23:32.275
why I had survived.

693
01:23:35.008 --> 01:23:38.846
I needed to look in your eyes
one last time.

694
01:23:42.169 --> 01:23:44.318
Well, I hope it was worth it.

695
01:23:46.342 --> 01:23:47.533
Mr. Silva...

696
01:23:47.566 --> 01:23:49.830
you are going to be transferred
to Belmarsh Prison...

697
01:23:49.909 --> 01:23:51.988
where you will be remainded
in custody...

698
01:23:52.595 --> 01:23:55.892
until the Crown prosecution service
deem you fit to stand trial...

699
01:23:56.543 --> 01:23:59.040
Say my name.
Say it.

700
01:23:59.058 --> 01:24:00.586
My real name.

701
01:24:01.815 --> 01:24:03.521
I know you remember it.

702
01:24:04.718 --> 01:24:09.011
Your name is on the memorial wall
of the very building you attacked.

703
01:24:09.788 --> 01:24:11.530
I will have it struck off.

704
01:24:12.131 --> 01:24:16.780
Soon, your past will be
as non-existent as your future.

705
01:24:17.273 --> 01:24:19.182
I'll never see you again.

706
01:24:22.104 --> 01:24:24.180
Did you know
what it does to you?

707
01:24:26.331 --> 01:24:28.622
Hydrogen cyanide?

708
01:24:40.994 --> 01:24:43.883
Look at what you've done,

709
01:24:44.627 --> 01:24:46.390
Mother...

710
01:25:24.556 --> 01:25:26.615
Let's me know what you recover
from its computers.

711
01:25:26.755 --> 01:25:28.591
Has he trasmitted the list?
If such, to who.

712
01:25:28.859 --> 01:25:31.394
- I want this resolved.
- Yes, ma'am.

713
01:25:37.765 --> 01:25:39.695
His name is
Tiago Rodriguez.

714
01:25:40.906 --> 01:25:42.510
He was a brilliant agent.

715
01:25:43.398 --> 01:25:46.930
But he started operating beyond
his brief hacking the Chinese.

716
01:25:47.261 --> 01:25:49.979
The hand over was coming up
and they were hunting him, so...

717
01:25:50.002 --> 01:25:51.135
I gave him up.

718
01:25:51.321 --> 01:25:52.813
I got six agents in return...

719
01:25:53.405 --> 01:25:54.988
and a peaceful transition.

720
01:25:55.013 --> 01:25:57.275
We should go, ma'am.
Board enquiry begins in 30-minutes.

721
01:25:58.282 --> 01:26:00.533
I want to know
what's on that computer.

722
01:26:13.363 --> 01:26:15.765
Now, looking
at Silva's computer...

723
01:26:16.499 --> 01:26:19.732
it seems to me he's done a number
of slightly unusual things.

724
01:26:20.283 --> 01:26:22.103
It's established
failed saved protocols...

725
01:26:22.289 --> 01:26:25.456
to wipe the memory if there's
any attempt to access certain files.

726
01:26:26.840 --> 01:26:29.359
Only about six people in the world
can program safe guides like that.

727
01:26:29.360 --> 01:26:31.522
Of course there are.
Can you get past them?

728
01:26:32.353 --> 01:26:34.074
I invented them.

729
01:26:37.261 --> 01:26:38.689
Right then.

730
01:26:40.087 --> 01:26:43.480
Let's see what you got for us...
Mr. Silva.

731
01:26:45.614 --> 01:26:47.286
We're in.

732
01:26:53.173 --> 01:26:54.016
Sir...

733
01:26:54.245 --> 01:26:55.760
What do you make of this?

734
01:27:01.072 --> 01:27:02.696
This is Omega site.

735
01:27:03.591 --> 01:27:05.628
What encrypted level it has.

736
01:27:07.223 --> 01:27:10.191
Looks like overstated code
to consider its true purpose.

737
01:27:12.052 --> 01:27:14.301
Security through obscurity.

738
01:27:15.744 --> 01:27:17.865
Ladies and gentlemen,
if I might have order.

739
01:27:19.564 --> 01:27:21.393
I'd like to begin
the proceedings.

740
01:27:23.179 --> 01:27:25.722
We are gathered today
to adjust some important issues

741
01:27:25.734 --> 01:27:29.191
concerning the future
of our national security.

742
01:27:34.703 --> 01:27:36.709
Going somewhere?

743
01:27:38.880 --> 01:27:42.459
So you believe your stewards of MI6
during the recent crisis

744
01:27:42.460 --> 01:27:43.821
has been up to scratch?

745
01:27:43.856 --> 01:27:47.249
Well, I believe we have
apprehended the responsible party

746
01:27:47.250 --> 01:27:48.775
undertaking all
the necessary steps

747
01:27:48.776 --> 01:27:51.805
to ensure that the sensitive
information is contained.

748
01:27:51.855 --> 01:27:54.764
Ugh! Such a job well done.

749
01:27:55.082 --> 01:27:56.794
I'm not saying
it all gone perfectly, but...

750
01:27:56.911 --> 01:27:59.361
You forgive me for not
putting up the banting.

751
01:27:59.831 --> 01:28:03.181
I find rather diffucult to overlook
the monumental security breaches

752
01:28:03.182 --> 01:28:06.797
and dead operatives which you were
singled handedly responsible.

753
01:28:09.570 --> 01:28:12.326
He's using a polymorphic engine
to mutate the code.

754
01:28:12.376 --> 01:28:14.910
Whenever I try to gain an access,
it changes.

755
01:28:15.124 --> 01:28:18.313
It's like solving the Rubik's cube
that's fighting back.

756
01:28:23.538 --> 01:28:24.985
Stop.

757
01:28:26.573 --> 01:28:28.010
Go into that.

758
01:28:34.817 --> 01:28:36.295
Granborough.

759
01:28:36.342 --> 01:28:37.795
Granborough Road,
it's an old...

760
01:28:38.189 --> 01:28:40.352
tube station
on the metropolitan line.

761
01:28:40.361 --> 01:28:42.272
Been closed for years.

762
01:28:44.060 --> 01:28:45.906
Use that as a key.

763
01:28:56.744 --> 01:28:58.725
Now, look. It's a map.

764
01:29:01.152 --> 01:29:03.160
It's London.

765
01:29:03.210 --> 01:29:05.659
Subterranean London.

766
01:29:07.209 --> 01:29:08.671
What's going on?

767
01:29:08.721 --> 01:29:10.133
Why the doors open?

768
01:29:20.733 --> 01:29:23.432
Can someone tell me how the hell
he got into our system?

769
01:29:27.439 --> 01:29:28.810
Oh, shit.

770
01:29:29.428 --> 01:29:32.014
Shit, shit, shit.

771
01:29:33.397 --> 01:29:35.977
He acted this.

772
01:29:42.491 --> 01:29:44.100
Oh, no.

773
01:29:51.857 --> 01:29:53.139
Q...

774
01:29:53.860 --> 01:29:55.484
He is gone.

775
01:30:04.695 --> 01:30:06.842
I'm on the stairway
of the low isolation.

776
01:30:07.068 --> 01:30:08.285
Are you with me, Q?

777
01:30:08.426 --> 01:30:10.396
I can hear you.
I'm looking for you.

778
01:30:21.057 --> 01:30:22.722
I've got him.
Tracking the location.

779
01:30:22.928 --> 01:30:24.108
Just keep looking forward.

780
01:30:24.956 --> 01:30:26.978
Enter the next service door
on your right.

781
01:30:33.575 --> 01:30:35.486
If you enter throught that door,
you should be in the tube.

782
01:30:36.416 --> 01:30:37.701
I'm in the tube.

783
01:30:39.299 --> 01:30:42.372
Bond, this isn't an escape.
This was years in the planning.

784
01:30:42.617 --> 01:30:45.296
He wanted us to capture him,
he wanted us to access his computers.

785
01:30:45.527 --> 01:30:46.446
It was all planned.

786
01:30:47.075 --> 01:30:50.294
Blowing up HQ,
only emergency protocols.

787
01:30:50.839 --> 01:30:53.044
And all we have retrieved
down here.

788
01:30:53.094 --> 01:30:53.977
I got all that.

789
01:30:54.707 --> 01:30:57.150
What it's got planned next
it worries me.

790
01:30:57.314 --> 01:30:58.579
The district line is the closest,

791
01:30:58.580 --> 01:31:00.952
there should be
a service door on your left.

792
01:31:02.032 --> 01:31:03.834
Got it.

793
01:31:07.502 --> 01:31:08.448
It won't open.

794
01:31:08.548 --> 01:31:09.998
Of course it will.
Put your back into it.

795
01:31:10.008 --> 01:31:12.391
Why don't you come down here
and put your back into it?

796
01:31:15.792 --> 01:31:17.597
No, it's studded.

797
01:31:18.366 --> 01:31:19.549
Not good.

798
01:31:20.052 --> 01:31:21.859
There's a train coming.

799
01:31:26.059 --> 01:31:28.266
Hmm. That's vexing.

800
01:31:41.080 --> 01:31:42.562
I'm through.

801
01:31:42.794 --> 01:31:43.825
I told you.

802
01:31:44.386 --> 01:31:47.142
We've alerted security.
Police are on the way.

803
01:32:24.158 --> 01:32:24.936
Where are you now?

804
01:32:25.510 --> 01:32:26.771
Temple tube station.

805
01:32:27.022 --> 01:32:29.449
Along with half of London.

806
01:32:33.231 --> 01:32:34.289
Oh I see. Here you are.

807
01:32:35.266 --> 01:32:37.178
I know where I am, Q.

808
01:32:38.114 --> 01:32:39.036
Where is he?

809
01:32:39.232 --> 01:32:41.666
Give us a second.
I'm looking for him.

810
01:32:49.673 --> 01:32:51.887
There's too many people.
I can't see him.

811
01:32:51.937 --> 01:32:53.436
Welcome to rush hour
on the tube.

812
01:32:54.281 --> 01:32:56.667
Something you don't know
much about.

813
01:33:06.781 --> 01:33:08.157
The train's leaving.

814
01:33:08.539 --> 01:33:10.009
Do I get on the train?

815
01:33:10.140 --> 01:33:13.216
Don't get on the train unless
he's on it. Give us a minute.

816
01:33:15.456 --> 01:33:17.169
Tell me if I get on the train.

817
01:33:22.560 --> 01:33:24.482
- Bond...
- What?

818
01:33:24.816 --> 01:33:26.362
Get on the train.

819
01:33:39.865 --> 01:33:41.686
He's keen to get home.

820
01:33:42.295 --> 01:33:43.864
Open the door, please.

821
01:33:46.252 --> 01:33:48.259
Open the door.

822
01:33:51.241 --> 01:33:53.880
I'm from Safety.
Carry on.

823
01:34:00.266 --> 01:34:03.314
- Where are you?
- Take a wild guess, Q.

824
01:34:03.928 --> 01:34:06.657
He's in disguise, now.
Disguised as a policeman.

825
01:34:29.141 --> 01:34:30.433
Where is he going?

826
01:34:30.760 --> 01:34:32.240
Where is he going?

827
01:34:39.209 --> 01:34:40.079
He's going for M.

828
01:34:40.201 --> 01:34:42.125
Tell Tanner.
Get her out of there.

829
01:34:42.150 --> 01:34:44.500
You overlooked
or chosen to ignore

830
01:34:44.693 --> 01:34:45.855
hard evidence...

831
01:34:46.472 --> 01:34:49.596
and consistenly,
almost obstantly...

832
01:34:49.878 --> 01:34:51.221
Silva has escaped.

833
01:34:51.732 --> 01:34:52.466
Bond's in pursuit.

834
01:34:52.717 --> 01:34:55.414
We need to get you to a secured
location immediately, ma'am.

835
01:34:55.496 --> 01:34:57.753
Like hell am I going
to show him my back.

836
01:34:58.046 --> 01:35:00.116
Are we straining your attention?

837
01:35:00.273 --> 01:35:03.891
No. Please, Minister.
Proceed.

838
01:35:11.793 --> 01:35:13.255
Excuse me.

839
01:36:36.118 --> 01:36:37.768
It's as if you insist on pretending

840
01:36:37.819 --> 01:36:40.263
we still live in the
golden age of espionage,

841
01:36:40.313 --> 01:36:43.519
when human intelligence
was the only resource available.

842
01:36:43.637 --> 01:36:45.982
Well, I find this rather
old-fashioned belief

843
01:36:46.246 --> 01:36:48.900
demonstrates
a reckless disregard for every...

844
01:36:48.950 --> 01:36:51.283
Excuse me, Minister.
I don't mean to interrupt but...

845
01:36:51.371 --> 01:36:52.962
Just for the sake of variety,

846
01:36:53.743 --> 01:36:56.320
might we actually hear
from the witness?

847
01:36:57.380 --> 01:36:58.874
Of course.

848
01:37:02.152 --> 01:37:03.906
Thank you.

849
01:37:32.123 --> 01:37:34.315
I won't miss next time,
Mr. Silva.

850
01:37:34.340 --> 01:37:35.254
Not bad.

851
01:37:35.363 --> 01:37:38.088
Not bad, James,
for a physical wreck.

852
01:37:38.382 --> 01:37:39.943
Oh, thank you.

853
01:37:40.402 --> 01:37:41.824
You caught me.

854
01:37:43.584 --> 01:37:46.723
Now, here's your prize.

855
01:37:46.773 --> 01:37:50.119
The latest thing
from my local toy store.

856
01:37:50.502 --> 01:37:53.433
It is called "radio".

857
01:38:01.477 --> 01:38:03.305
I do hope that wasn't for me.

858
01:38:03.663 --> 01:38:04.707
No.

859
01:38:05.501 --> 01:38:06.630
But that is.

860
01:38:58.323 --> 01:38:59.342
Chairman, Ministers...

861
01:38:59.517 --> 01:39:01.815
Today I've repeatedly heard how

862
01:39:02.133 --> 01:39:04.547
irrelevant my department
has become.

863
01:39:04.722 --> 01:39:07.219
Why you we need agents
for Double-O section.

864
01:39:07.220 --> 01:39:09.416
Isn't that all rather quaint?

865
01:39:10.296 --> 01:39:13.443
Well, I suppose I see a different
world than you do.

866
01:39:14.571 --> 01:39:18.049
And the truth is that
what I see frightens me.

867
01:39:19.745 --> 01:39:23.482
I'm frightened because our enemies
are not longer known to us.

868
01:39:24.256 --> 01:39:26.268
They do not exist on the map.

869
01:39:26.367 --> 01:39:28.218
They're not nations.

870
01:39:28.647 --> 01:39:30.086
They are individuals.

871
01:39:31.681 --> 01:39:33.571
But look around you,
who do you fear?

872
01:39:34.200 --> 01:39:37.836
Can you see a face,
a uniform, a flag? No.

873
01:39:38.675 --> 01:39:40.792
Our world is not
more transparent now.

874
01:39:41.017 --> 01:39:42.477
It's more opaque.

875
01:39:42.911 --> 01:39:44.687
It's in the shadows.

876
01:39:45.758 --> 01:39:48.092
That's where we must
do battle.

877
01:39:49.098 --> 01:39:52.236
So, before you declare
us irrelevant, ask yourselves:

878
01:39:53.385 --> 01:39:56.055
How safe do you feel?

879
01:40:00.470 --> 01:40:02.117
Just one more thing to say.

880
01:40:02.720 --> 01:40:05.364
My late husband was
a great lover of poetry.

881
01:40:05.781 --> 01:40:07.394
And, um...

882
01:40:07.444 --> 01:40:09.358
I suppose some of it sunk in,

883
01:40:09.383 --> 01:40:11.529
despite my best intentions.

884
01:40:12.160 --> 01:40:13.478
And here today,
I remember this.

885
01:40:13.479 --> 01:40:16.399
I think, from Tennyson.

886
01:40:19.007 --> 01:40:21.778
We are not now that strength

887
01:40:22.467 --> 01:40:25.180
which in old days
moved earth and heaven.

888
01:40:26.514 --> 01:40:28.460
That which we are, we are.

889
01:40:29.492 --> 01:40:32.499
One equal temper
of heroic hearts.

890
01:40:33.436 --> 01:40:37.590
Made weak by time and fate,

891
01:40:38.222 --> 01:40:41.316
but strong in will...

892
01:40:41.365 --> 01:40:44.702
to strive, to seek, to find

893
01:40:45.118 --> 01:40:48.385
and not to yield.

894
01:42:11.028 --> 01:42:12.294
Move.

895
01:42:12.319 --> 01:42:14.915
Move. Move.

896
01:42:54.723 --> 01:42:56.469
007, what the hell
are we doing?

897
01:42:56.585 --> 01:42:57.887
You're kidnapping me.

898
01:42:57.912 --> 01:43:00.176
That would be one way
of looking at it.

899
01:43:02.438 --> 01:43:04.840
Too many people are dying
because of me.

900
01:43:05.201 --> 01:43:07.139
If you wants you,
he's gonna have to come and get you.

901
01:43:07.140 --> 01:43:09.580
We've been one step behind Silva
from the start.

902
01:43:09.630 --> 01:43:11.991
It's time to get out in front
and change the game.

903
01:43:12.854 --> 01:43:14.570
And I'm to be the bait?

904
01:43:16.787 --> 01:43:18.245
All right.

905
01:43:18.822 --> 01:43:21.133
Just us.
No one else.

906
01:43:22.091 --> 01:43:24.382
Q, I need help.

907
01:43:24.519 --> 01:43:26.314
I'm tracking the car.
Where are you going?

908
01:43:26.594 --> 01:43:28.834
I got M.
We're about to disappear.

909
01:43:29.225 --> 01:43:30.163
What?

910
01:43:30.364 --> 01:43:31.521
I need you to lay
a trail of breadcrums

911
01:43:31.522 --> 01:43:33.823
impossible to follow
for anyone except Silva.

912
01:43:33.848 --> 01:43:35.347
You think you can do it?

913
01:43:37.020 --> 01:43:38.631
I'm guessing
this isn't strictly official.

914
01:43:38.807 --> 01:43:40.151
Not even remotely.

915
01:43:40.322 --> 01:43:43.485
So much for my promising
career in espionage.

916
01:43:51.740 --> 01:43:54.429
Well, I'm not hiding in there
if that's your brilliant plan.

917
01:43:54.430 --> 01:43:56.487
We're changing vehicles.

918
01:43:57.076 --> 01:44:00.366
The trouble with company cars
is they have trackers.

919
01:44:09.868 --> 01:44:12.806
And I suppose that's completely
inconspicuous.

920
01:44:13.744 --> 01:44:15.187
Get in.

921
01:44:37.507 --> 01:44:39.347
It's not been accountable, is it?

922
01:44:41.296 --> 01:44:43.134
Are you going to complain
the whole way?

923
01:44:43.239 --> 01:44:45.043
Oh, go on and eject me.

924
01:44:45.093 --> 01:44:46.383
See if I care.

925
01:44:48.942 --> 01:44:50.188
Where are we going?

926
01:44:51.943 --> 01:44:52.860
Back in time.

927
01:44:54.068 --> 01:44:56.072
Somewhere we'll have
the advantage.

928
01:44:58.129 --> 01:44:59.258
It's a fine line.

929
01:44:59.861 --> 01:45:02.340
If a breadcrum's too small
then he might miss it.

930
01:45:02.481 --> 01:45:04.854
Too big and Silva
will smell the rat.

931
01:45:04.904 --> 01:45:07.774
That's what you think, even Silva
will be able to spot that?

932
01:45:08.147 --> 01:45:09.525
He's the only one who could.

933
01:45:12.438 --> 01:45:13.517
Sir...

934
01:45:16.514 --> 01:45:17.745
What are you doing?

935
01:45:17.770 --> 01:45:19.177
We just monitoring...

936
01:45:19.427 --> 01:45:22.826
Creating a false tracking signal
for Silva to follow.

937
01:45:23.122 --> 01:45:24.262
Well, sir...

938
01:45:25.195 --> 01:45:27.086
Excellent thinking.
Get them isolated.

939
01:45:27.179 --> 01:45:28.985
Send him on the I89.
It's the direct route.

940
01:45:29.075 --> 01:45:31.194
You can monitor his progress
more accurately

941
01:45:31.579 --> 01:45:33.697
and confirm it
with the traffic cameras.

942
01:45:33.747 --> 01:45:35.824
But what if PM finds out?

943
01:45:36.931 --> 01:45:38.583
Then, they're all bugged.

944
01:45:39.148 --> 01:45:40.813
Carry on.

945
01:46:22.929 --> 01:46:24.405
This is where you grew up?

946
01:46:25.627 --> 01:46:26.841
Mmhh...

947
01:46:29.340 --> 01:46:31.298
How old were you
when you died?

948
01:46:34.744 --> 01:46:36.668
You know the answer to that.

949
01:46:38.839 --> 01:46:40.763
You know the whole story.

950
01:46:49.250 --> 01:46:51.786
Orphans always make
the best recruits.

951
01:46:57.900 --> 01:46:59.548
The storm's coming.

952
01:47:59.534 --> 01:48:01.372
Christ...

953
01:48:03.635 --> 01:48:05.379
I wonder
you never came back.

954
01:48:59.334 --> 01:49:00.750
James...

955
01:49:00.922 --> 01:49:02.594
James Bond.

956
01:49:02.644 --> 01:49:04.269
Good God.

957
01:49:05.721 --> 01:49:07.373
You're still alive.

958
01:49:08.954 --> 01:49:11.329
Nice to see you too.

959
01:49:12.480 --> 01:49:14.541
M... this is Kincade.

960
01:49:15.203 --> 01:49:17.499
Kincade is keeping here
since I was a boy.

961
01:49:17.580 --> 01:49:20.338
- Please to meet you, Emma.
- Mr. Kincade.

962
01:49:21.808 --> 01:49:25.173
You're a tad late. They sold the place
when they thought you were dead.

963
01:49:25.238 --> 01:49:27.027
Seems they were wrong.

964
01:49:27.926 --> 01:49:29.189
What are you doing here?

965
01:49:29.661 --> 01:49:31.489
Some men are coming to kill us.

966
01:49:32.868 --> 01:49:34.430
We're gonna kill them first.

967
01:49:36.251 --> 01:49:38.599
Then we'd better get ready.

968
01:49:40.143 --> 01:49:41.647
Do we still have
a gun room?

969
01:49:45.401 --> 01:49:49.897
They sold a lot to a collector
from Idaho or some such place.

970
01:49:50.009 --> 01:49:52.537
They were shipped up
weeks ago.

971
01:49:53.154 --> 01:49:58.467
There's just your father's
old hunting rifle.

972
01:49:59.336 --> 01:50:01.520
We couldn't let that go.

973
01:50:07.417 --> 01:50:08.818
And this is what we've got.

974
01:50:10.363 --> 01:50:13.418
There might be a couple of sticks
of dynamite from the quarry.

975
01:50:14.454 --> 01:50:17.956
But if all else fails,
sometimes...

976
01:50:18.448 --> 01:50:21.717
the old ways
are the best.

977
01:50:26.773 --> 01:50:29.303
So, who are we
supposedly fighting?

978
01:50:29.734 --> 01:50:31.680
No "we", Kincade.

979
01:50:32.288 --> 01:50:34.133
This is not your fight.

980
01:50:34.158 --> 01:50:37.337
Try to stop me,
you jumped-up little shit.

981
01:50:39.008 --> 01:50:42.604
Now, remember what I taught to you.
Don't let it pull to the left.

982
01:50:43.924 --> 01:50:45.652
I'll do my best.

983
01:50:54.459 --> 01:50:56.752
What did you say
you did for a living?

984
01:51:12.113 --> 01:51:13.428
Emma...

985
01:51:14.299 --> 01:51:16.339
I brought you some things.

986
01:51:19.180 --> 01:51:21.105
The nights get cold here.

987
01:51:21.967 --> 01:51:23.646
Thank you, Mr. Kincade.

988
01:51:25.290 --> 01:51:26.636
It's a beautiful old house.

989
01:51:26.719 --> 01:51:28.139
She is.

990
01:51:28.431 --> 01:51:30.333
And like all great ladies,

991
01:51:30.915 --> 01:51:33.237
she still has
her secrets ways.

992
01:51:33.912 --> 01:51:35.374
Let me show you this.

993
01:51:40.469 --> 01:51:41.644
A priest hole.

994
01:51:41.695 --> 01:51:44.070
Yes, from
Reformation times.

995
01:51:44.587 --> 01:51:46.234
The tunnel leads
under the moor.

996
01:51:46.284 --> 01:51:48.986
If you get in danger,
this is the place to come.

997
01:51:49.920 --> 01:51:51.957
The night I told him
his parents have died...

998
01:51:52.840 --> 01:51:55.420
he's hidden here
for two days.

999
01:51:57.315 --> 01:51:58.860
But he did come out.

1000
01:51:59.403 --> 01:52:01.337
He was no boy anymore.

1001
01:52:02.452 --> 01:52:04.517
We must get on.

1002
01:54:04.864 --> 01:54:07.140
I fucked this up,
didn't I?

1003
01:54:08.480 --> 01:54:09.813
No.

1004
01:54:11.608 --> 01:54:13.422
You did your job.

1005
01:54:18.586 --> 01:54:20.328
I read your obituary of me.

1006
01:54:21.988 --> 01:54:24.283
- And?
- Appaling.

1007
01:54:25.133 --> 01:54:26.843
Yeah, I knew you'd hate it.

1008
01:54:29.159 --> 01:54:31.258
It called you <i>'An example
of the British fortitude.'</i>

1009
01:54:32.208 --> 01:54:33.582
I think that was all right.

1010
01:54:39.088 --> 01:54:40.405
Are you ready?

1011
01:54:40.414 --> 01:54:43.040
I was ready before
you're were born, son.

1012
01:56:03.323 --> 01:56:05.181
Welcome to Scotland.

1013
01:57:21.878 --> 01:57:23.716
You dropped something?

1014
01:57:49.955 --> 01:57:51.101
Are you hurt?

1015
01:57:51.143 --> 01:57:52.689
Only my pride.

1016
01:57:52.873 --> 01:57:54.697
I never was a good shot.

1017
01:57:59.619 --> 01:58:00.647
He's not here,

1018
01:58:01.627 --> 01:58:02.851
and he's not here.

1019
01:58:37.437 --> 01:58:39.608
Always good
at making an entrance.

1020
01:58:40.654 --> 01:58:42.526
You two, go to
the kitchen. Now!

1021
01:59:07.140 --> 01:59:08.800
Go behind the yard.

1022
01:59:51.468 --> 01:59:53.582
Go to the chapel.
Use the tunnel.

1023
02:01:14.587 --> 02:01:17.750
Everyone listen to me.
Don't you dare touch M.

1024
02:01:17.800 --> 02:01:19.343
She's mine.

1025
02:01:36.054 --> 02:01:38.447
And your friends
come out and say 'hello'?

1026
02:02:45.207 --> 02:02:48.106
Come on. This way.

1027
02:03:45.313 --> 02:03:47.606
I always hated this place.

1028
02:03:57.647 --> 02:03:59.813
Are you getting warm?

1029
02:05:27.702 --> 02:05:29.723
Just make sure
Bond is dead.

1030
02:05:33.180 --> 02:05:35.590
Now it's me and her.

1031
02:07:33.544 --> 02:07:37.360
You see what comes of all
this running around, Mr. Bond?

1032
02:07:38.263 --> 02:07:40.943
All this jumping
and fighting.

1033
02:07:40.969 --> 02:07:42.459
It's exhausting.

1034
02:07:45.876 --> 02:07:47.081
Relax.

1035
02:07:49.037 --> 02:07:50.743
You need to relax.

1036
02:08:10.234 --> 02:08:12.197
Well, mother's calling.

1037
02:08:14.016 --> 02:08:16.436
I'll give her
a goodbye kiss for you.

1038
02:10:35.429 --> 02:10:37.083
Of course.

1039
02:10:37.408 --> 02:10:39.128
It had to be here.

1040
02:10:41.695 --> 02:10:43.849
It had to be this way.

1041
02:10:44.896 --> 02:10:46.529
Thank you.

1042
02:10:46.687 --> 02:10:47.880
- I can't find it, though.
- No.

1043
02:10:52.227 --> 02:10:53.275
Please.

1044
02:10:54.019 --> 02:10:55.425
Don't.

1045
02:11:10.182 --> 02:11:11.775
You're hurt. You're hurt.

1046
02:11:16.733 --> 02:11:19.014
What have they
done to you?

1047
02:11:19.498 --> 02:11:21.619
What have they
done to you?

1048
02:11:53.836 --> 02:11:55.221
Free the both of us.

1049
02:11:55.903 --> 02:11:57.196
Free the both of us.

1050
02:11:59.025 --> 02:12:00.795
With the same bullet.

1051
02:12:02.067 --> 02:12:03.107
Do it.

1052
02:12:04.085 --> 02:12:05.370
Do it!

1053
02:12:06.862 --> 02:12:08.451
Only you can do it.

1054
02:12:09.281 --> 02:12:10.372
Do it!

1055
02:12:52.911 --> 02:12:54.445
Last rat standing.

1056
02:13:05.056 --> 02:13:06.707
007.

1057
02:13:06.769 --> 02:13:07.896
What took you so long?

1058
02:13:08.545 --> 02:13:09.545
Oh, I...

1059
02:13:09.546 --> 02:13:11.762
got into some
deep water.

1060
02:13:27.356 --> 02:13:28.822
I suppose it's...

1061
02:13:29.782 --> 02:13:32.471
too late to hang around
and fret.

1062
02:13:38.394 --> 02:13:40.440
Well, I'm game if you are.

1063
02:13:50.633 --> 02:13:53.301
I did get one thing right.

1064
02:15:17.388 --> 02:15:18.336
Wow!

1065
02:15:19.891 --> 02:15:22.241
I didn't even know
you could come up here.

1066
02:15:23.431 --> 02:15:25.445
I hate to waste a view.

1067
02:15:25.495 --> 02:15:27.511
I can see why.

1068
02:15:29.307 --> 02:15:32.047
I thought you were going back
out on active service.

1069
02:15:33.463 --> 02:15:35.099
I declined.

1070
02:15:36.867 --> 02:15:38.320
You said it yourself.

1071
02:15:38.923 --> 02:15:40.913
Field works
are not for everyone.

1072
02:15:41.814 --> 02:15:44.554
If it helps,
I feel a lot safer.

1073
02:15:49.943 --> 02:15:51.666
Her will was read today.

1074
02:15:52.717 --> 02:15:54.456
She left you this.

1075
02:16:06.477 --> 02:16:09.139
Maybe it was her way of telling you
to take a desk job.

1076
02:16:10.257 --> 02:16:11.852
Just the opposite.

1077
02:16:15.125 --> 02:16:16.847
Thank you.

1078
02:16:35.397 --> 02:16:37.848
You know, we've never formally
been introduced.

1079
02:16:41.663 --> 02:16:43.372
My name is Eve.

1080
02:16:44.008 --> 02:16:45.573
Eve Moneypenny.

1081
02:16:46.140 --> 02:16:48.798
I look forward to our time together,
Miss Moneypenny.

1082
02:16:49.394 --> 02:16:50.637
Me too.

1083
02:16:51.224 --> 02:16:53.854
I'm sure we will have
one or two clear shaves.

1084
02:16:55.748 --> 02:16:56.910
Good morning, 007.

1085
02:16:57.190 --> 02:16:59.852
- Good morning, Tanner.
- He will see you now.

1086
02:17:15.058 --> 02:17:16.284
How's the arm, sir?

1087
02:17:16.780 --> 02:17:17.558
What?

1088
02:17:17.881 --> 02:17:19.260
Oh, it's fine.

1089
02:17:19.441 --> 02:17:20.721
It will get better.

1090
02:17:20.857 --> 02:17:22.301
All pretty shocking
for someone

1091
02:17:22.302 --> 02:17:24.906
unused to field work.

1092
02:17:26.735 --> 02:17:28.575
So, 007...

1093
02:17:28.996 --> 02:17:31.122
Lots to be done.

1094
02:17:34.456 --> 02:17:36.641
Are you ready
to get back to work?

1095
02:17:38.295 --> 02:17:39.895
With pleasure, M.

1096
02:17:42.432 --> 02:17:44.030
With pleasure.

1097
02:17:45.590 --> 02:17:50.590
Sync and corrections by pinex
www.subscene.com
